 "documents": {
  "https://legis.example/de/hb1.html": "<html><body><h1>House Bill 1</h1><p>AN ACT relating to water quality (fixture).</p><p>Section 1. Short title. This act may be cited as the Fixture Water Quality Act, and it sets the standards that public water systems in the state shall meet.</p><p>Section 2. Standards. The department shall adopt rules setting the largest amount of each listed contaminant that a public water system may deliver, and shall review those rules every five years.</p></body></html>",
  "https://legis.example/de/hb1-eng.html": "<html><body><h1>House Bill 1, as engrossed</h1><p>AN ACT relating to water quality (fixture).</p><p>Section 1. Short title. This act may be cited as the Fixture Water Quality Act, and it sets the standards that public water systems in the state shall meet.</p><p>Section 2. Standards. The department shall adopt rules setting the largest amount of each listed contaminant that a public water system may deliver, and shall review those rules every three years after a public hearing.</p><p>Section 3. Reports. Each system shall publish an annual report of its test results.</p></body></html>",
  "https://legis.example/private/sb2.html": "<html><body><p>Section 1. Not to be fetched: robots.txt disallows this path for every agent, so the text layer never asks for it.</p></body></html>",
  "https://mi.example/sb1.htm": "<html><body><h1>Senate Bill 1</h1><p>A bill to provide for library access (fixture).</p><p>Sec. 1. This act shall be known and may be cited as the fixture library access act, and it applies to every public library that receives state aid in any fiscal year.</p><p>Sec. 2. A public library shall keep its main reading room open to the public for at least forty hours each week.</p></body></html>",
  "https://mi.example/hb4001.htm": "<html><body><h1>House Bill 4001</h1><p>A bill relating to water quality (fixture).</p><p>Sec. 1. This act may be cited as the Fixture Water Quality Act, and it sets the standards that public water systems in the state shall meet.</p><p>Sec. 2. The department shall adopt rules setting the largest amount of each listed contaminant that a public water system may deliver, and shall review those rules every five years.</p></body></html>"
